<title>UK: BP, Zeneca up after ADR strength.</title>
<headline>BP, Zeneca up after ADR strength.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum Co Plc, Zeneca Group Plc and other international stocks rose sharply in pre-market trading on Friday after strength in their ADRs in the U.S. yesterday.</p>
<p>BP was up 12-1/2p at 695-1/2 by 0815 GMT after its ADRs rose $1-3/4 to $138-1/8, Zeneca rose 29-1/2p to 16.60 stg after its ADRs rose $2-3/4 to $83-1/4 And Shell Transport &amp; Trading Co rose 10p to 994, after its ADRs rose $3-3/4 to $171.</p>
<p>Yesterday the Dow in New York posted its second-biggest ever gain in point terms to close 126.87 points up at 6,473.64.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
